.TH SUBMIT 1.SH NAMEsubmit \- run a file of commands with parameters.SH SYNOPSIS\fBsubmit\fRname [parameter ...].SH DESCRIPTION\fBsubmit\fRruns the commands in the file\fIname\fB.sub\fRone after another, printing each line before it runs it.  Name the filewithout its suffix:\fBsubmit demo alpha\fRruns\fBdemo.sub\fR.\fRIn the file,\fB%1\fR,\fR\fB%2\fRand on stand for the parameters given after the name..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fREvery line goes to a module called\fBshell\fR,\fRthe one your own OS-9 brings; with no\fBshell\fRresident the lines are printed and nothing runs.\fB/dd/SYS/login\fRloads yours from\fB/h1\fRwhen your system is mounted there..SH SEE ALSOrepeat